    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0526" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.01/7½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just talked with Mr.
                    Norman Davis<anchor n="45" xml:id="d362-f1"/> over the telephone. He informed me
                    that the understanding with the British Embassy with regard to Mexico was as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>That in view of pressure which was being brought to bear on the British
                    Government to recognize Mexico, that Government had decided not to recognize
                    until we should do so; that we would keep them advised of any important steps
                    which we might take looking toward recognition, in order that British action
                    might follow ours.</p>
                <closer><signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enry</hi>] P. F[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">letcher</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d362-f1" n="45" xml:id="d362-f1-content">
                <p>Alberto J. Pani, Mexican Secretary of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
